          "post_id": "497304",
          "text": "<p>Consider the machine $M^{\\prime}$ :<br><br><img alt=\"\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The language recognized by $M^{\\prime}$ is:<br>&nbsp;</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$\\left\\{w \\in\\{0,1\\}^* \\mid\\right.$ $w$ HAS AN EVEN NUMBER OF $0$s AND AN EVEN NUMBER OF $1$s$\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\left\\{w \\in\\{0,1\\}^* \\mid\\right.$ $w$ HAS AN ODD NUMBER OF $0$s AND AN EVEN NUMBER OF $1$s$\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\left\\{w \\in\\{0,1\\}^* \\mid\\right.$ $w$ HAS AN EVEN NUMBER OF $0$s AND AN ODD NUMBER OF $1$s$\\}$<br>&nbsp;</li><li>$\\left\\{w \\in\\{0,1\\}^* \\mid\\right.$ $w$ HAS AN ODD NUMBER OF $0$s AND AN ODD NUMBER OF $1$s$\\}$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "A",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "subject": "Theory of Computation",
          "day": "Day 131"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "497309",
          "text": "<p>CONSIDER TWO PROBLEMS: $L_1$ IS A DECIDABLE LANGUAGE, AND $L_2$ IS A RECURSIVELY ENUMERABLE (R.E.) BUT NOT DECIDABLE LANGUAGE. LET $L_3$ BE ANOTHER LANGUAGE.<br><br>WHICH ONE OF THE FOLLOWING STATEMENTS IS <strong>FALSE</strong>?<br>&nbsp;</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>IF $L_3$ IS R.E. AND ITS COMPLEMENT $\\bar{L}_3$ IS ALSO R.E., THEN $L_3$ IS DECIDABLE.<br>&nbsp;</li><li>IF $L_3$ IS REDUCIBLE TO $L_1$, THEN $L_3$ IS DECIDABLE.<br>&nbsp;</li><li>IF $L_2$ IS REDUCIBLE TO $L_3$, THEN $L_3$ IS UNDECIDABLE.<br>&nbsp;</li><li>IF $L_1$ IS REDUCIBLE TO $L_3$, THEN $L_3$ IS DECIDABLE.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "D",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "subject": "Theory of Computation",
          "day": "Day 131"
        },
        {
          "post_id": "497305",
          "text": "<p>CONSIDER A DFA OVER $\\Sigma=\\{a, b\\}$ THAT ACCEPTS A STRING $w$ IF AND ONLY IF $w$ SATISFIES BOTH OF THE FOLLOWING CONDITIONS:</p><ol><li>THE NUMBER OF $a^{\\prime} \\mathrm{S}$ IN $w$ IS ODD.<br>&nbsp;</li><li>THE VALUE OF $\\left(n_a+2 \\cdot n_b\\right)(\\bmod 3)=0$, WHERE $n_a$ IS THE COUNT OF $a$'S AND $n_b$ IS THE COUNT OF $b$'S.</li></ol><p>WHAT IS THE MINIMUM NUMBER OF STATES THAT THIS DFA WILL HAVE?</p>",
